# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sampler window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sampler and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-sampler-1 throughout: SB builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after SB's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# SPt: the TIMING twin of the SP arm: c2-packed-tp4-speed-sprewarm (c2-packed-tp4-speed: both verify audits OFF, the tail caps ON, no instruments, no stall watch)
# plus QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_PREWARM=1: the pinned sampler (the T1 audit's sample_rows call: the sampler all-gather, untilize and ArgMax over 248,320 columns, two 32-row sample_tiles calls for 64 rows) runs ONCE in the packed block's eager warm forward, before the verify capture, and its result is discarded; nothing sampler-related is in the trace or in any replay, and nothing is read back or compared per round.
# Run it after the five repeats on the diag twin pass (a hang here costs the card reset): read the round time and the coding
# decode rate against c2-packed-tp4-speed on the same image, which costs the arm's extra work per replay (in-trace) or nothing per
# replay (prewarm). The coding tests: single-user coding, concurrent4_code, concurrent4_code_equal, concurrent8_code.
# Duration (estimate): 25 min. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sampler-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-sprewarm
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent8_code
